# Fixed 2026-10-07, defect 458, lane b14-check: the shape beside it on the
# other half of the pair. A `lease` with an argument too many, or none, is
# told its count and nothing more, measured so on the base, and the cell it
# initialises is still a lease cell, so its `end_lease` is quiet. This case
# pins it; it was not red on the base.

function main()
    x = "abc"
    c: cstr @= x.lease(1)  #~ builtin_shape
    d: cstr @= lease()  #~ builtin_shape
    end_lease(@c)
    end_lease(@d)
